# Assembly Coding Standards

## Code Organization
Reference [src/main.asm](mdc:src/main.asm) for proper code organization:
- Use cc65 assembler directives
- Follow memory map defined in [src/memory.cfg](mdc:src/memory.cfg)
- Use meaningful labels and comments
- Document register usage

## Memory Layout
Memory configuration is defined in [src/memory.cfg](mdc:src/memory.cfg):
```asm
MEMORY {
    ZP:      start = $0000, size = $0100, type = rw;  // Zero Page
    STACK:   start = $0100, size = $0100, type = rw;  // Stack
    RAM:     start = $0200, size = $FD00, type = rw;  // Main RAM
    VECTORS: start = $FFFA, size = $0006, type = ro;  // Interrupt vectors
}
```

## Code Style
- Use 4-space indentation
- Document all interrupt handlers
- Include hardware initialization code
- Use clear and consistent naming
- Comment register usage

## Error Handling
- Include proper error checking
- Handle invalid memory accesses
- Document error conditions
- Implement recovery procedures

## Build Process
Use `make asm` to:
1. Compile assembly with ca65
2. Link according to memory configuration
3. Generate hex file for FPGA memory
